      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Update, 2026-10-02: findings re-measured and worked (bean `n5be`, issue #1838)",
      "prov:value": "1. **No longer holds.** The page has a \"Filter this table\" box (bean `0fua`, the standalone table filter). There is still no A–Z jump. With the order fixed (2), the filter is the way in.\n2. **Fixed.** Rows sort by the displayed term, with the notation as a tie-break. Measured: 0 descending pairs over 55 rows, against 4 before. Before, each ledger restarted the alphabet (\"Agent, Actor, …\").\n3. **No longer holds** (#1594). There are 0 literal backticks, and inline code renders as `<code>` and links.\n4. **Fixed.** The term cell prints the ledger relative to the sub-graph (`glossary-ledger.json` or `bootstrap/glossary-ledger.json`). The `#key` is already the `notation` fact, and the link still goes to the full path. The first column is 20rem (was 26rem). Below 800 px every auto-docs row stacks the term above its definition at full width. Measured at 390: `scrollWidth` 390, and the definition is 296 px wide (was 214 px beside an 89 px term).\n5. **Fixed.** The one-row sibling list is dropped. Its count moves into the lede (\"Sub-graph `cat-harness/glossary`, 55 entries.\"). The scope now appears twice, as the h1 id and the lede path, and these are two different facts.\n6. **Fixed.** The declaration comment no longer quotes a count. It had said 44 while the page showed 46, then 48, then 55.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0fua"
      ]
    }
  ]
